On-demand engines for filee-cli.

Filee's app downloads FFmpeg, Pandoc, Ghostscript, calibre and LibreOffice from Settings -> Engines. The command line
had no way to do that, so those conversions failed unless the engine was on the PATH. This patch:

 * adds `filee engines list|install|remove` and installs the engines a conversion needs before it runs (`convert`, and
   per batch in `watch`), with `--no-install` to turn that off. Progress and messages go to stderr; --json stays clean.
   Concurrent processes take turns through a lock file in the engines folder. Empty files never trigger a download.
 * adds the two engines upstream does not offer on macOS to engines.json: FFmpeg (Martin Riedl's release build, kind
   `zip-programs` with ffprobe as a companion file) and Ghostscript (conda-forge's gs, kind `conda-unix`), and the two
   install kinds that unpack them. Every download is checked against its SHA-256 before it is unpacked.
 * tests for the new install kinds, companions, and path safety.

Drop it when upstream ships an equivalent.

